# =============================================================================
#  Docker build context  —  WO-22 (PKG-05)
# =============================================================================
#  Both images build from the repository root, so this one file governs both.
#
#  This is not only a speed optimisation. Next's standalone output tracer copies
#  whatever it finds next to the app, and it was verified to pull `.env.local`
#  and the `apps/web/.env` symlink straight into `.next/standalone/`. Without
#  the env rules below, a built image would carry the production Neon URL and
#  JWT_SECRET in a layer — readable by anyone who can `docker pull` it, and
#  still readable after a later layer deletes the file.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets. Keep this block first and do not weaken it. --------------------
#
#  IMPORTANT: .dockerignore is NOT .gitignore. Docker matches each pattern
#  against the full path relative to the build context, so a bare `.env`
#  matches ONLY the root `.env` — it does not match `apps/web/.env`. Every
#  pattern here needs an explicit `**/` prefix to apply at depth. This was
#  originally written with git's semantics in mind and left `apps/web/.env`
#  and `apps/web/.env.*` in the build context.
#
#  It surfaced as a build failure rather than a leak, and only by luck:
#  `apps/web/.env` is a symlink to the root `.env.local`, which *was* excluded,
#  so Docker copied a dangling symlink and `next build` died on stat(). Had it
#  been a real file, it would have gone into an image layer instead — silently.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.render.example
!.env.vercel.example
.envrc
**/.envrc
.sentryclirc
**/.sentryclirc
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/secrets/
**/credentials/

# --- Database dumps: member PII, and large. ----------------------------------
backups/
*.dump
*.dump.gpg
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile. -------------------------
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# --- Build outputs. A host .next/ leaking in produces a container serving a
#     stale build that no source change explains. ----------------------------
.next
**/.next
out
dist
build
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Go build artefacts. Rebuilt in the builder stage. -----------------------
bin/
apps/api/server
apps/api/app
**/*.test
**/*.out

# --- Not needed to build or run. ---------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.githooks
.gitleaks.toml
docs
*.md
!apps/web/README.md
LICENSE
test-results
playwright-report
playwright/.cache
coverage
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.agents
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
